.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
the parts of an icon-list specific to the evas canvas. 

generic parts are in icon_list. gevas-specific parts are in gevas_bind.
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "int evas_ext_evt (\fBicon_list\fP * il, int x, int y, int b, theme_area_event_type t, theme_area_event_modifiers m, void * data, \fBicon\fP ** ext, void ** rp)"
.PP
propagate mouse-clicks to concerned extension plug-ins 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
what the extension said (or NOIR_NOTFOUND 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIx\fP - window-relative x-position of click 
.br
\fIy\fP - window-relative y-position of click 
.br
\fIb\fP - mouse-buttons 
.br
\fIt\fP - the event-type (press, release, double-click, ...) 
.br
\fIm\fP - modifiers 
.br
\fIdata\fP - the session 
.br
\fIext\fP - where to return the extension that consumed the event, or NULL 
.br
\fIrp\fP - where the extension can store a return value (pointer)
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBicon\fP* evas_ext_find (\fBicon\fP ** areas, const char * name)"
.PP
find extension plugin by name. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIareas\fP - the linked list of extensions 
.br
\fIname\fP - the name of the extension we're looking for
.RE
.PP

.SS "int evas_ext_upd (\fBicon_list\fP * il, \fBfile_info\fP * fi)"
.PP
redraw all extensions in icon-list 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
an error-code < 0, or a count of queried extensions 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP icon-list 
.br
\fIfi\fP the file-info of the current directory
.RE
.PP

.SS "int evas_file_activate (\fBicon_list\fP * il, \fBicon\fP * i, Evas * evas)"
.PP
open-file animation. 
.PP
will determine whether to run t->ani_open_file() or t->ani_open_app(). will return result of \fBfile_activate()\fP. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - icon-list 
.br
\fIi\fP - icon 
.br
\fIevas\fP - evas, or NULL for auto
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBicon\fP* evas_find_first_selected (\fBicon_list\fP * il)"
.PP
find first selected icon. 
.PP
called from \fBgevas_bind::gevas_keyed()\fP. used as a fallback when an icon should be selected via keyboard, but isn't. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list
.RE
.PP

.SS "int evas_find_icon_by_string (\fBicon_list\fP * il)"
.PP
find first icon whose name matches il->find. 
.PP
called from \fBgevas_bind::gevas_keyed()\fP. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list
.RE
.PP

.SS "int evas_find_icon_by_string_chk (\fBicon_list\fP * il, size_t * l)"
.PP
got key in evas. 
.PP
check whether find-string has timed out. if so, start a new one, else add to existing one. called from \fBgevas_bind::gevas_keyed()\fP. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIl\fP - where length of the find-string (il->find) lives
.RE
.PP

.SS "char* evas_get_file_from_icon (void * data, \fBicon\fP * i)"
.PP
get file-tag from an icon. 
.PP
called from \fBgevas_bind::gevas_keyed()\fP, \fBgevas_bind::gevas_clicked()\fP and \fBevas_open_folder()\fP. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIdata\fP - the session 
.br
\fIi\fP - the icon to get the file from
.RE
.PP

.SS "int evas_icon_chg_event (\fBicon_list\fP * il, \fBicon\fP * i, \fBfile_info\fP * fi)"
.PP
update the pictogram/thumbnail of an icon. 
.PP
called from \fBicon_view::icon_view_evt()\fP. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
an error-code. anything but NOIR_FAIL should be regarded as a suggestion to redraw the icon-view. 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list to update 
.br
\fIi\fP - the icon to update 
.br
\fIfi\fP - the file to update
.RE
.PP

.SS "void evas_icon_set_state (\fBicon_list\fP * il, \fBicon\fP * i, icon_state s)"
.PP
set state (selected, normal, . 
.PP
..) of an icon. if the icon-factory provides a function \fBicon_set_state()\fP, that function will be called. if it returns TRUE (or there is no such function), all elements suitable for the desired state will be shown; all others will be hidden. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIi\fP - the icon 
.br
\fIs\fP - the desired state
.RE
.PP

.SS "void evas_keyed_icon (\fBicon_list\fP * il, int new)"
.PP
focus new icon by keyboard. 
.PP
called from \fBevas_find_icon_by_string()\fP and by \fBgevas_bind::gevas_keyed()\fP. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fInew\fP - the icon that should now be selected, or -1 for none
.RE
.PP

.SS "void evas_open_folder (\fBnoir_sess\fP * ns, \fBicon_list\fP * il, \fBicon\fP * i, Evas * evas)"
.PP
open-folder animation. 
.PP
will run theme->ani_open_folder() for the given icon. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIns\fP - session 
.br
\fIil\fP - icon-list 
.br
\fIi\fP - icon 
.br
\fIevas\fP - evas, or NULL for auto
.RE
.PP

.SS "int evas_rename_icon (\fBnoir_sess\fP * ns, \fBicon\fP * i)"
.PP
rename the file represented by a given icon. 
.PP
normally called when the label is double-clicked. called from \fBgevas_bind::gevas_clicked()\fP. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIns\fP - the session 
.br
\fIi\fP - the icon
.RE
.PP

.SS "void icon_el_data_dst (void * data)"
.PP
destruct data (Evas-Object) of an icon-element. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIdata\fP - the Evas-Object
.RE
.PP

.SS "int icon_list_get_selection (void * data, \fBicon_list\fP * il)"
.PP
return current selection of icon-list 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIdata\fP - the session 
.br
\fIil\fP - the icon-list
.RE
.PP

.SS "int icon_list_set_selection (\fBicon_list\fP * il)"
.PP
set selection in icon-view. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - icon-list
.RE
.PP

.SS "void icon_move (\fBicon\fP * i, int x, int y)"
.PP
move an icon. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIi\fP - the icon to be moved 
.br
\fIx\fP - new x-position 
.br
\fIy\fP - new y-position
.RE
.PP

.SS "int pointer_on_icon_p (\fBicon_list\fP * il, \fBicon\fP * i, int x, int y)\fC [inline]\fP"
.PP
check whether mouse-pointer is over a given icon. 
.PP
this means 'within the icon's bounding box, within an element's bounding box, on a non-transparent pixel'. called from \fBicon_list::icon_list_get_icon_at()\fP. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
TRUE or FALSE. 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIi\fP - the icon 
.br
\fIx\fP - mouse-x, window-relative 
.br
\fIy\fP - mouse-y, window-relative
.RE
.PP

.SS "int pointer_on_iconlabel_p (\fBicon\fP * i, int x, int y)"
.PP
check whether mouse-pointer is over a given icon's label. 
.PP
called from \fBgevas_bind::gevas_clicked()\fP. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
TRUE or FALSE. 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIi\fP - the icon 
.br
\fIx\fP - mouse-x, window-relative 
.br
\fIy\fP - mouse-y, window-relative
.RE
.PP

.SS "int sb_chk (\fBicon_list\fP * il, \fBicon\fP * i, int x, int y)"
.PP
check whether mouse is over scrollbar. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
SB_BAR for 'over bar', SB_PGUP for 'above', SB_PGDN for 'below bar'. 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIi\fP - the scroll-bar 
.br
\fIx\fP - mouse-x (icon-list relative) 
.br
\fIy\fP - mouse-y (icon-list relative)
.RE
.PP

.SS "void sb_update (\fBicon_list\fP * il, int scrolled)"
.PP
update scroll-bar and icon-list. 
.PP
called from icon-list and \fBgevas_bind::gevas_icon_list_resized()\fP. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIscrolled\fP - was the region damaged only (FALSE), or scrolled as well (TRUE)?
.RE
.PP

.SS "int selection_update (\fBnoir_sess\fP * ns, \fBclient_funs\fP * skip)"
.PP
copy selection to all views in a session. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIns\fP - the session 
.br
\fIskip\fP - the calling client (don't call setter on that, it already knows)
.RE
.PP

